# Singularity/Apptainer definition for the Fields Model submission image — v2.2 (allsm).
#
# v2.2 over v2.1 (training-config changes; the v2.1 self-contained-nvcc fix carries over unchanged):
#   - PRIMARY TARGET is now the 32B: default --experiment olmo_32b_fp8, default global batch 1.5M
#     (1,572,864 — divides cleanly for WORLD_SIZE 2/3/4/6 at cp=4), --max-tokens-per-rank 16384 (cp=4),
#     --olmo-ac-budget 0.4, --keep-last 1.
#   - LR scheduler: cosine with alpha_f=0.1 (5e-5 -> 5e-6 floor), warmup 0.03.
#   - The 7B uses the SAME 1.5M batch now (one batch for both sizes).
#   - Default dataset: chankhavu/smolmo-sft-olmocore-pretokenized (subdir olmocore).
#   - The four topology vars (WORLD_SIZE / GLOBAL_RANK / MASTER_ADDR / MASTER_PORT) are a HARD requirement.
#
# v2.1 fix (retained): ships its OWN real nvcc (CUDA-13.0 pip wheels: nvcc + nvvm/cicc + crt) first on
# PATH (/opt/fields/bin) so the container never resolves a HOST nvcc — the noexec-host-nvcc PermissionError
# that crashed every rank at the first torch.compile. Re-verified on v2.2 (docker + Singularity, cold compile).
#
# Bootstraps from the LOCAL docker image (chankhavu/olmo3-sft-v2.2:cu130-allsm) and bakes the real
# credentials (fields/SECRETS.json) into /app/SECRETS.json so the container needs no `-e` on the
# NII/ABCI Singularity cluster. The docker image itself is pushed WITHOUT secrets; the secrets live
# ONLY in this locally-built .sif — never push this .sif to a shared/public registry.
#
# Build (from repo root, so %files paths resolve):
#   bash fields/build_sif.sh olmo-sft-v2.2-allsm.sif chankhavu/olmo3-sft-v2.2:cu130-allsm fields/olmo-sft-v2.2-allsm.def
# NOTE: apptainer/SingularityCE 1.5.1 bundles mksquashfs 4.7.5, which crashes on this ~12GB rootfs
# ("Bug in orderer"/SIGSEGV). build_sif.sh works around it via sandbox + system mksquashfs.
#
# Run — the 4 topology vars are REQUIRED (even single-node); a bare call runs the default 32B fp8 shape.
# Single node (8 GPUs):
#   singularity run --nv --containall \
#     --bind /scratch/$USER/training:/tmp \
#     --env WORLD_SIZE=1,GLOBAL_RANK=0,MASTER_ADDR=127.0.0.1,MASTER_PORT=29400 \
#     olmo-sft-v2.2-allsm.sif --no-remote-shell
# Multi-node (2/3/4/6 nodes): per-node GLOBAL_RANK, shared MASTER_ADDR:PORT, shared --bind volume — see MULTINODE.md.

Bootstrap: docker-daemon
From: chankhavu/olmo3-sft-v2.2:cu130-allsm

%files
    # Bake real credentials into the .sif (HF_TOKEN + WANDB_API_KEY). secrets_loader reads
    # /app/SECRETS.json; a same-named env var still wins at runtime.
    fields/SECRETS.json /app/SECRETS.json

%runscript
    # Mirror the docker ENTRYPOINT explicitly so `singularity run <sif> <flags>` == train.py.
    exec python /app/train.py "$@"

%labels
    org.fields.entrypoint /app/train.py
    org.fields.base chankhavu/olmo3-sft-v2.2:cu130-allsm
    org.fields.secrets baked
    org.fields.version v2.2

%help
    Fields Model SFT image v2.2 (Olmo-3, 32B-primary). Entrypoint: python /app/train.py. Ships its own
    nvcc so it never depends on the host's. The four topology vars (WORLD_SIZE/GLOBAL_RANK/MASTER_ADDR/
    MASTER_PORT) are required. Bind a host dir to /tmp (defaults write there) and pass train.py flags after
    the .sif path. A bare run uses the default olmo_32b_fp8 at its fitting shape (cp=4, ac 0.4, 1.5M batch).
